Replying to my own note is bad form, especially since I have been 
inactive for so long, but getting more artsy would probably be even 
better. Are not metaphors legal in lojban? To wit,
     "She was an LED in an era of candles".
     "She was a 21st century prisoner in an XXth century jail".
etc. But Oren's right. Idioms translated word for word don't always 
work.Even when you look for an equivalent expression, you have to have 
the context before you can know the connotation. A literal translation 
might work, though, if you sense the word "time" as "(proper?) era" and 
"was born" as "existed", it comes out pretty clean, I think. I leave the 
hard work for someone more qualified, but I think the key words are
   http://jbovlaste.lojban.org//dict/zasti
   http://jbovlaste.lojban.org//dict/cedra
but I could be unqualified to make even that judgement


